From: Gauthier Piarrette <gauthierpiarrette@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32: Do not fail CredEnumerateW() when the host store has no match.

Adapted for CrossOver 26.3 from gauthierpiarrette/highball-engine
commit a2b10db8b86f4ed5f02855a41fa7c6ad4d3cbfb6 (patch 0019). The code
is unchanged. This is a downstream fix, not a WineHQ backport or a
game-specific change; WineHQ has the same two lines today.

CredEnumerateW() collects credentials from the registry, then from the
host's store through mountmgr. On macOS that store is the Keychain, and
mountmgr's search_credentials() returns STATUS_NOT_FOUND when no
Keychain item matches the filter. CredEnumerateW() only forgave
ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED, the answer where there is no host store, so on
macOS a filter that matched registry credentials but no Keychain item
failed the whole call with ERROR_NOT_FOUND and the registry matches
were dropped. On Windows, a filter that matches stored credentials
returns them.

A program that keeps its own generic credentials and looks them up by
prefix therefore never found them: a sign-in library that reads its
device key and tokens with a filtered CredEnumerateW() made a new
device key on every start and asked the user to sign in again each
time.

An empty answer from the host is now treated like an unsupported host:
the registry count decides, and ERROR_NOT_FOUND is still returned when
nothing matched anywhere. host_enumerate_credentials() returns before
touching the count, length or buffer on that path.

diff --git a/dlls/advapi32/cred.c b/dlls/advapi32/cred.c
index dd8d7ce..6cfce5e 100644
--- a/dlls/advapi32/cred.c
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/cred.c
@@ -1059,7 +1059,8 @@ BOOL WINAPI CredEnumerateW(LPCWSTR Filter, DWORD Flags, DWORD *Count, PCREDENTIA
     if (ret == ERROR_SUCCESS)
     {
         ret = host_enumerate_credentials(Filter, NULL, NULL, &len, Count);
-        if (ret == ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED) ret = ERROR_SUCCESS;
+        /* nothing matching in the host's store is not a failure, the registry may hold the matches */
+        if (ret == ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED || ret == ERROR_NOT_FOUND) ret = ERROR_SUCCESS;
     }
     if (ret == ERROR_SUCCESS && *Count == 0)
         ret = ERROR_NOT_FOUND;
@@ -1085,7 +1086,7 @@ BOOL WINAPI CredEnumerateW(LPCWSTR Filter, DWORD Flags, DWORD *Count, PCREDENTIA
             if (ret == ERROR_SUCCESS)
             {
                 ret = host_enumerate_credentials(Filter, *Credentials, buffer, &len, Count);
-                if (ret == ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED) ret = ERROR_SUCCESS;
+                if (ret == ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED || ret == ERROR_NOT_FOUND) ret = ERROR_SUCCESS;
             }
         }
         else ret = ERROR_OUTOFMEMORY;
